{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB06626 - MONDO_5005",
  "verbalization": "Axitinib is associated with Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma through a mechanistic pathway involving Everolimus, a known inhibitor of mTOR, which is a key regulator of cell growth and survival in renal cell carcinomas. The evidence suggests that Axitinib may be repurposed for Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma, as it shares a common pathway with Nonpapillary Renal Cell Carcinoma, which also interacts with Everolimus. The integration of these pathways implies that Axitinib could exert a therapeutic effect on Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma by targeting the mTOR signaling cascade, which is a recurring mechanism in renal cell tumors. The presence of a direct indication from Axitinib to Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma, along with the indirect pathway through Everolimus, supports the hypothesis that Axitinib may have a role in the treatment of this disease. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though further validation through clinical trials or additional molecular studies would be necessary to confirm its therapeutic potential.",
